course: dictionary
lesson: 14213
title: Mummification: a word from history and science
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one topic, such as history or science. «Mummification» is one of these. Look for the clues around it: a dead body, and something kept for a very long time. Those clues tell you the word is about preserving a body.
explain: «The museum guide explained the mummification of the pharaoh, step by step.» The word has a clue inside it: mummy. A mummy is a preserved body, so mummification is the process that makes one. Test your meaning in the sentence: the guide explained how a dead body was preserved. It still makes sense.
explain: Mummification can also happen by itself. «The walker found a body in the peat bog, and the cold, wet ground had kept it from rotting.» Nobody did this on purpose; the place did it. Both kinds of mummification stop a body from rotting, and that is the key idea.
fact: Mummification means preserving a dead body so that it does not rot.
fact: The ancient Egyptians practised mummification: they removed organs, dried the body with natron, wrapped it in linen bandages and placed it in a coffin.
fact: Natural mummification happens in very dry, cold or boggy places, where a body is preserved without human help.
fact: Mummification is an uncountable noun, so you do not usually say «mummifications».
fact: In science, dryness and cold stop the decay that makes a body rot.
exercise: What does mummification mean? | Wrapping a present in paper | Burying a body under a large stone | *Preserving a dead body so that it does not rot | Making a body grow back
exercise: «The Egyptians used natron to dry the body during mummification.» What was natron used for? | *To dry the body | Painting the coffin | To light the tomb | To wash the children
exercise: Which kind of place can cause natural mummification? | Busy city street | Crowded market | *Cold, dry or boggy ground | Hot, wet jungle
test: Why did the ancient Egyptians practise mummification? | They wanted to make bandages for the river | *They believed the body was needed in the afterlife | They were trying to grow taller | They wanted to turn bodies into stone
test: Mummification stops a body from doing what? | Smiling | *Rotting | Growing | Flying
exam: Which sentence uses mummification correctly? | *«Mummification kept the body from rotting for thousands of years.» | «I had a mummification for lunch.» | «The mummification was a fun day at the beach.» | «The mummifications ran across the field.»
